    "turn_text": "I never went to be famous. I went because I wanted to learn tips that I could bring back into my career, my speaking circuit, and teach other people how to be successful business people to attract more money into their lives and their businesses. And Donald Trump and I liked each other. The minute we met each other, we were very much alike. He was a billionaire. I was not. But we were very similar in, we never quit. We never give up. We always say what we mean. We're very direct. We're very authentic. And I really fell in love with him, his family. And I was so grateful for the opportunity. So, when President Trump asked me, Donald Trump at the time, asked me if I would put my three careers on hold at the time, Caleb. I was a professional speaker, a business coach, and I had a radio show here in Des Moines. He asked me if I'd put my careers on hold to help him get elected, because you know, as well as anybody knows, that if you're going to be the next President of the United States, you have to win Iowa.",
